Scientific status correction
----------------------------
Final wording: "Outcome A: verified sectorial Fedoryuk applicability
framework."  The exact Kerr normal form meets the local analytic
prerequisites on a cut canonical domain avoiding the pole and turning points
only when its progressive paths are separately verified.  The local simple
and close/double models are identified.  The full family of required domains
and progressive paths is not constructed, so no proved sectorial theorem,
global connection coefficient, or Bargmann spectral condition is claimed.

Local direction derivation
--------------------------
For Q0=a_j(y-y_j)^m(1+O(y-y_j)),
S_j=2 sqrt(a_j)(y-y_j)^((m+2)/2)/(m+2) to leading order.  With the convention
Stokes: Re S_j=0 and anti-Stokes: Im S_j=0, the implemented rays are

theta_S(k)=[(2k+1)pi-arg(a_j)]/(m+2),
theta_A(k)=[2k pi-arg(a_j)]/(m+2),  k=0,...,m+1.

Changing sqrt(a_j) to -sqrt(a_j) sends S_j to -S_j and does not change either
geometric ray set.

